{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "metadata": {
    "id": "murmur-fx-master-chain",
    "name": "FX MASTER CHAIN",
    "author": "Patchwork Eight Engineering",
    "description": "A lush detuned pad demonstrating GATE 10/11's basic effect set (docs/ROADMAP.md) working together in the master bus's 4 slots the way a real mix would use them: Eq (gentle low-shelf cut to declutter the low end, a touch of high-shelf air) -> Reverb (GATE 11's nuanced/massive redesign: an 1.8-size hall with extended low-frequency ring via reverbLowRatio, faster high-frequency decay via reverbHighRatio, high diffusion/density for a smooth non-metallic tail, and gentle late-tank modulation for movement) -> Compressor (a slow, gentle glue -- low ratio, moderate threshold, not audibly pumping) -> Limiter (a quiet -0.3dB safety ceiling, doing essentially nothing to a well-gain-staged patch like this one, exactly as a limiter should when nothing is actually clipping). Written directly in schema v2 (envelopes[]/lfos[] arrays) since this preset was authored after the GATE 5 migration, not before it.",
    "category": "pad",
    "moods": [
      "lush",
      "spacious",
      "polished",
      "massive"
    ],
    "genres": [],
    "tags": [
